1. DATASET SOURCES & REFERENCES

EARTHNEX AI is designed to bring together Earth observation and environmental information from publicly available scientific data resources.

Primary Data Sources:

1. NASA Earthdata
   
   - Earth observation and satellite-based scientific datasets.
   - Environmental and climate-related data discovery.
   - Reference: https://earthdata.nasa.gov/

2. NASA Open APIs
   
   - Publicly accessible NASA data services and API documentation.
   - Reference: https://api.nasa.gov/

3. NASA Earth Science Resources
   
   - Earth system observations and scientific data resources.
   - Reference: https://science.nasa.gov/earth-science/

Environmental Data Categories:

- Climate and atmospheric conditions.
- Temperature and humidity.
- Land and surface observations.
- Water resources and hydrological information.
- Environmental and geographical indicators.

Data Usage Note: These are the project's referenced data ecosystems. Individual datasets and APIs are considered integrated only where an active connection has been implemented and verified in the prototype.

