3. THREAT MODEL & DATA RELIABILITY

EARTHNEX AI considers the following potential risks:

Potential Threat| Mitigation Approach
Unavailable external APIs| Error handling and alternative data-source support
Incomplete datasets| Data availability checks
Outdated environmental observations| Display available observation dates and timestamps
Incorrect or inconsistent data| Data validation and preprocessing
Location inaccuracies| Geographical validation
Unauthorized access| Appropriate API and backend access controls
Misinterpretation of predictions| Clearly distinguish observations from estimated outputs

Data Reliability: The platform depends on the availability, accuracy, resolution and update frequency of external scientific data providers. Results should be interpreted with their source and temporal context.

Security Considerations:

- Protect API credentials and avoid exposing private keys.
- Validate incoming data and API responses.
- Handle external service failures safely.
- Avoid presenting unverified environmental information as confirmed facts.

